Feature: EN 1996 structural scene
  The masonry snapshot and its check report project to a deterministic, locale-free 3D scene, a set of 2D diagrams and drag handles.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - openings are cut out of the wall zones: Given the wall with a window and a door pier When the scene is projected Then the volumes of the bottom, middle and top zone add up to the wall volume minus the openings times the thickness And entity "wall-openings:lintel-win-1" is a lintel over the window
  - utilisation colours the wall zones: Given the compliant clay wall and its check report When the scene is projected Then the largest zone ratio equals the utilisation of the compression check And the middle zone ratio equals the utilisation of the mid-height compression check And the bottom zone carries more utilisation than the top zone
  - the bond is explicit and checked: Given the compliant clay wall When the scene is projected Then entity "wall-north:units" lies on the hidden bond layer in running bond And a unit length of 80 mm violates the overlap of max(0.4 hu, 45 mm) and is drawn in error style
  - concentrated loads spread at 60 degrees: Given the wall with a concentrated beam load of bearing length 200 mm When the scene is projected Then the spreading zone is 200 mm wide at the top and 200 mm plus h over the square root of 3 wide at mid-height
  - laterally loaded walls show their yield-line pattern: Given the compliant clay wall held on two, three and four sides When the scene is projected Then the yield-line regions number two, three and four and tile the wall
  - handles write document leaves: Given the compliant clay wall When the length handle of "wall-north" is dragged to 6.012 m Then one write sets "walls[id=wall-north].lengthM" to 6.0 m And the opening, floor bearing, eccentricity and bearing length handles write their current value at their anchor
  - diagrams agree with the closed forms: Given the compliant clay wall and its check report When the diagrams are built Then the Φ markers equal the profile of the compression checks And an independent Python oracle reproduces the mesh volumes, Φ_m of Annex G, the f_k power law with its caps, the 60° spreading, the isotropic yield load 24 m over l squared and the tabulated fire thickness
  - check stations colour the wall zones and units are cut at the openings: Given a wall with a window and a door When the check engine evaluates the wall Then the compression check carries three stations of the field "wall-phi" at the bottom, middle and top sections with the reduction factor Phi And the lateral flexure check carries 11 stations of the field "wall-lateral" along the height And each zone is tinted per vertex from the stations and its binding equals its section station And every masonry unit that meets an opening is cut to the remaining wall rectangles
  - the fire time track binds the tabulated thickness demand of every fire class: Given the compliant clay wall of 0.365 m thickness with group 1 clay units and general purpose mortar When the scene is projected Then the fire track spans R 30 to R 240 in seconds and the field "fire-demand@90" on the wall equals the tabulated 0.13875 m at mu_fi 0.7 divided by 0.365 m
  - The wall deflects under wind, cracks outside the middle third and shows its flanges and bearing stress blocks: Given a committed wall with a wind load case, a shear flange and a concentrated load When the structural scene is projected Then a one-metre strip carries a ramped deflected shape equal to the closed-form pinned beam line of the masonry stiffness And the cracked depth is zero up to t over six and three e minus t over two beyond it And the flange and the rectangular bearing stress block under the concentrated load are separate entities bound to their checks
  - every check outcome is drawn by exactly one owner: Given any example document and its check report When the checks are routed Then every check belongs to the wall, concentrated load, chase, movement joint, opening, bar or member row its id names, or to a declared design case, or to the document badge for the integrity and system families And the owner stands in the scene and the focus of the check resolves to it
  - every numeric field has a grip: Given the snapshot schema of the masonry walls, openings, members, loads, chases and joints When the handles of the example documents are collected Then each numeric field is written by a geometric grip or a gauge of twenty schema steps per metre, or has a documented exemption
  - the concentrated load enhancement is plotted over a1 over H: Given a wall of height 2.75 m with a beam bearing of 0.04 m2 at a1 of 0.5 m When the diagrams are built Then the curve beta equals the product of one plus 0.3 a1 over H and 1.5 minus 1.1 A_b over A_ef limited to the smaller of 1.25 plus a1 over 2 H and 1.5 and to at least 1 And the design point sits at a1 over H of 0.18 on the curve and drags the distance a1
  - the outcome diagram draws the rest: Given a wall with checks of families that have no dedicated diagram When the diagrams are built Then one bar per such check shows its utilisation against the limit at 1 and no drawn family appears twice
